<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David Ben-Gurion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1886">1886</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as David Grün</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Ben-Gurion was the Zionist labour leader who declared Israel's independence on 14 May 1948 and served as its first prime minister, leading the state through the 1948 war, the mass immigration that doubled its population, and the building of its institutions and army. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, he had headed the Jewish Agency under Mandatory <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, and after leaving office he retired to a kibbutz in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negev">Negev</a>; he remains Israel's founding statesman.</p></div>
